{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1339318-need-clarification-on-titanic-virtues","id":1339318,"title":"Need clarification on Titanic virtues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-04T01:31:40-07:00","id":1339318,"title":"Need clarification on Titanic virtues","content":"Hello everyone, my first post here and on the the question.<br /> <br /> A thing that confuses me about Titanic virtues is, what kind of actions they represent, what does a being representing Submission do etc? It\u00b4s a bit confusing for me as english is a second language for me. I can\u00b4t seem to figure out the difference between the four Titanic virtues and what some of these want to accomplish and represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25445-awenei","name":"Awenei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T01:43:33-07:00","id":1339319,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the Titanic Virtues are... Kind of weird. I personally don't use them and would honestly run most Titans as not really having Virtues at all, as looking at them, many of the Virtues are attempts to say slightly similar things. But I suppose I can try to help explain them.<ul><li>Fecundity - The desire to spread their Purview. A Titan of, say, the Fire Purview with Fecundity would wish to see the influence of Fire spread throughout the World, though perhaps without destroying it. A Fecundity Fire Titan would have seen humanity make fireplaces in their homes and would be pleased, as Fire is spreading throughout the World.</li> <li>Rapacity - The desire to consume. A Rapacity Fire Titan would wish to burn all before it, leaving nothing in its wake but ash.</li> <li>Submission - This one is confusing, as the Titan itself is not acting submissive, but is absorbing things within itself. A Water Submission Titan would seek to flood the world and wear away all things until all that remains is water.</li> <li>Dominance - A Dominance Titan may not wish to destroy the World with its Purview, but does desire its influence to spread through the World.</li> </ul><br /> As I said, I don't really like them. They feel a bit... Like how Virtues worked in 1e, and in the context of 1e they'd be great, but they feel odd with how Virtues work in 2e.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you can probably just ignore them. I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T01:58:22-07:00","id":1339321,"title":"","content":"Honestly those were the Virtues i used in 1e that the writers picked up, and the original point of Dominance and Submission were the Titans\u2019 relationship to the \u201cGreater Titan\u201d which doesn\u2019t really apply in 2e.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d suggest just using Rapacity (drive to destroy) and Fecundity (drive to create) as the default self-explanatory pair, swapping in Pantheon Virtues as appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T02:03:43-07:00","id":1339322,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help and insight, really appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25445-awenei","name":"Awenei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T02:05:11-07:00","id":1339323,"title":"","content":"Thank for the help and insight. Really appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25445-awenei","name":"Awenei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T16:41:19-07:00","id":1339464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1339318-need-clarification-on-titanic-virtues?p=1339321#post1339321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly those were the Virtues i used in 1e that the writers picked up, and the original point of Dominance and Submission were the Titans\u2019 relationship to the \u201cGreater Titan\u201d which doesn\u2019t really apply in 2e.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d suggest just using Rapacity (drive to destroy) and Fecundity (drive to create) as the default self-explanatory pair, swapping in Pantheon Virtues as appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be a drive to create or a drive to expand?\ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T17:39:13-07:00","id":1339478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1339318-need-clarification-on-titanic-virtues?p=1339464#post1339464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be a drive to create or a drive to expand?\ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>As I conceived of it in 1e, it was drive to create, but I get making it expand in 2e to play up the relationship to their signature purview.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, one could use the expansion of a titan\u2019s signature purview as the inherent overlap of their creative and destructive impulses (and thus the thing that can pull them out of Virtue extremity)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T06:27:51-07:00","id":1339580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Awenei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1339318-need-clarification-on-titanic-virtues#post1339318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, my first post here and on the the question.<br /> <br /> A thing that confuses me about Titanic virtues is, what kind of actions they represent, what does a being representing Submission do etc? It\u00b4s a bit confusing for me as english is a second language for me. I can\u00b4t seem to figure out the difference between the four Titanic virtues and what some of these want to accomplish and represent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My personal take on the Submission Virtue:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Gods use their powers to dominate and govern their respective purviews.<br /> <br /> Titans use their powers to serve and protect their purviews.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Titan submits itself to the role of acting as a force of nature. While their traitorous progeny sought to seize control of such forces and bend them to their own will. The Titans represent their purviews in their truest expression; free from the ridiculous morality and skewed perceptions placed on them by mortals and gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}